<%- include('partials/head') %>
  <body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

    <main>
      <h2>Getting Involved</h2>

      <figure>
        <img src="/img/hackathon.jpg" alt="People working on laptops together at a hackathon">
        <figcaption>Volunteers at the Wikimania 2014 hackathon (<a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wikimania_2014_-_Day_1_-_Hackathon_participants_05.JPG">photo</a>)</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <article>
        <h3>You don't have to be an expert</h3>
        <p>
          A lot of people think you need to be a senior developer to help with open
          source. You don't. Some of the most useful help has nothing to do with code.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Report a bug when something breaks, with the steps to make it happen again</li>
          <li>Fix a typo or unclear line in the instructions</li>
          <li>Translate the app into another language</li>
          <li>Answer someone else's question</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Changing the code</h3>
        <p>Once you're ready to help with code, the steps on GitHub are pretty simple.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Fork the project, which makes your own copy.</li>
          <li>Make your change and test it.</li>
          <li>Open a pull request, which asks the owner to add your change to the real project.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The owner might ask for changes first. That's normal, and it's a good way to learn.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Be a good guest</h3>
        <p>
          Read the README before jumping in. Many projects also have a contributing
          guide that explains how they like things done. Most maintainers are
          volunteers, so being patient and polite goes a long way.
        </p>
      </article>

      <section class="sources">
        <h3>Sources</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://opensource.guide/how-to-contribute/">Open Source Guides, How to Contribute</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/exploring-projects-on-github/contributing-to-a-project">GitHub Docs, Contributing to a project</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
  </body>
</html>
